    "killington": {
      "status": "ok",
      "resort": "Killington",
      "adapter": "powdr",
      "updatedAt": "2026-04-27 05:47:19",
      "note": "Good morning, Beast family, What a weekend. Thanks to everyone who came out and soaked up the sun with us over the past few days. We’re kicking off our final week of seven-day operations with a beautiful spring day on tap. Expect plenty of sunshine, with temperatures climbing into the low 50s up top and pushing toward 60 at the base. It’s shaping up to be one of those classic late-season days where it just feels good to be out there. With temperatures staying above freezing overnight, conditions will be soft right from the start. Expect true spring skiing across the mountain, with smooth, forgiving turns early and surfaces gradually bumping up as the day goes on. Superstar continues to shine, with great coverage and bumps that will keep things interesting lap after lap. Our grooming team is focused on preserving snow where it matters most this time of year. Superstar will remain ungroomed to maintain depth, while Skyelark down through Lower Bittersweet will offer some early corduroy before transitioning into softer spring conditions. It should be another great setup for long, laid-back laps. Over in Skyehawk, our spring park remains in play with a handful of features still firing. Whether you’re hiking for laps or taking the quick ride up, it’s a fun mid-mountain zone to mix things up. The Superstar Six is scheduled to spin at 9:00 a.m. and will run through 4:00 p.m. Please note that there is currently no beginner terrain available, and late-season conditions exist across the mountain. On another note, our trail crew in the Bike Park is already hard at work getting things ready for summer. Please stay off bike trails until opening day on May 22. We appreciate your help as we transition seasons. Let’s make it a great day out there. -Josh Operating Day: 167 Season passes for 2026/27 are now on sale! Lock in the lowest price on Beast 365 or Winter Unlimited passes with lots of perks, plus free skiing & riding for the rest of this spring. And there's more good news for families: Youth & Child pass pricing has been significantly reduced for next season, with over $300 in savings available on Beast 365 access. Lifts The Superstar Six will operate seven days a week from 9:00 a.m. to 4:00 p.m. on Monday through Friday, from 8:00 a.m. to 5:00 p.m. on Saturdays, and from 8:00 a.m. to 4:00 p.m. on Sundays. Starting on May 3rd, the Superstar Six will be open Friday through Sunday while conditions allow. The Tubing Park presented by bubly is closed for the season. Uphill Travel Uphill travel is now closed for this season. Please visit killington.com/uphill for full information on our uphill travel policies. MOUNTAIN SERVICES Parking & Shuttles Parking is available at our K-1 Lodge and at the top of Killington Road. Please respect signage and allow our parking staff to assist you on your trip to the slopes. Shuttle service is available from 7:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. midweek and 6:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. on weekends and holidays through Sunday, May 3rd unless otherwise stated in this report. Winter car camping and overnight parking is only available in the lot across from Skyeship Lodge, though please note that the Skyeship Lodge is closed for the season. See details here . Lodge Services All lodges listed here are open daily from 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. on weekdays and 7:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. on weekends/peak dates*. K-1 Lodge Breakfast: Served starting at 8:30 a.m. on weekdays. Lunch: Served from 10:30 a.m. - 2:00 p.m. on Monday through Thursday with limited grill station offerings. Brew Bar (2nd floor): Closed for the season. Will re-open during the weekend dependent on weather conditions. K-1 Pub (3rd floor): Closed for the season. Rentals & Killington Sports at K-1: Open 30 minutes before lifts until 30 minutes after lifts. Demos & Tuning: Available via the K-1 Rental Shop daily through May 3rd. Beast 365, Unlimited, and Midweek Pass holders can receive 50% off demo rentals. Guest Services: 1st floor - Open 30 minutes before lifts until 30 minutes after lifts. 2nd floor location is closed for the season. Superstar Umbrella Bar: Open at 11:00 a.m. from Friday - Sunday offering beer, wine, liquor, and cocktails. Serving lunch on the weekends at the nearby outdoor grill from 10:30 a.m. - 2:30 p.m. (weather permitting). Ramshead Lodge - Closed for the season. Bear Mountain Lodge - Closed for the season. Snowshed Lodge - Closed for the season. Snowshed Demos & Tuning remains open seven days a week, providing tuning services for guests and Season Tune holders. Demos also available with more options at K-1. Skyeship Lodge - Closed for the season. On-Mountain Dining Options : Peak Lodge – Closed for the season. Jerk Jamaican Mountain Grill – Closed for the season. Ledgewood Yurt – Closed for the season. Mountain services are subject to change. Please check here daily before making your lunch and lodge choices. Winter Lift Tickets and rentals must be purchased online at this link . Check to see if your pass is good to go using our Online Pass Checker . Find our Season Pass FAQs by clicking here . Season passes for summer 2026 and winter 26/27 are now on sale! Buy now . Have a ticketing question? Our text number ( 802-523-2202 ) is the best way to get it answered quickly, but please note that we cannot process transactions via text. Have a season pass question? Call 1-800-621-MTNS or email seasonpass@killington.com Please visit Killington.com/cancellation for more details on our cancellation policy. Killington is a cashless resort. We accept all major credit cards as well as Apple, Google, and Samsung Pay. *No remaining Peak Dates during winter 2025/26. We strive to have the most up-to-date and accurate snow report, but errors can happen from time to time. If you have feedback or a correction for us, please share it here.",
