      "resort": "Copper Mountain",
      "adapter": "powdr",
      "updatedAt": "2026-04-27 05:00:00",
      "note": "Good morning and Happy Monday Copper faithful. Welcome to day 1 of extended spring operations! Don't cry because it's almost over, smile because it's still happening. We've picked up 4\" of new snow over the last 24 hours, with about half of that falling after the lifts closed yesterday. Snow flurries will continue off and on today with some additional accumulation expected. Temps will rise to the mid 30s at mid-mountain with light westerly winds gusting to 20mph. Snow picks up slightly overnight into tomorrow, with additional snow showers possible all week. We're still skiing and riding on 3 chairlifts until the end, serving up 17 trails and almost 2300 vertical feet for you to enjoy. Visit Camp Hale in Center Village or the Aerie for all of your food and bev needs. Please note there is no beginner terrain available during our last week of the winter season. Have a great day and see you out there!",
